# Development standards

Follow these skills as the source of truth. Do not invent APIs or desktop patterns from memory.

Project skills (`.cursor/skills/`): `pi-dev`, `electron-development`.

## Mac delivery (`Document/DEVELOPMENT.md`)

- Every Mac packaging entry point must produce one Universal application/DMG/ZIP containing both x64 and arm64. Do not restore separate default architecture packages; legacy architecture scripts are Universal aliases.
- Windows adaptation and acceptance are outside the current development scope.
- Preserve native unpack/Universal merge rules, pass the full local gates, and freeze build inputs while packaging. Local packaging must disable signing/notarization and publishing. Follow `Document/DEVELOPMENT.md` for offline cache preparation and artifact acceptance.

## Pi (`pi-dev`)

- Read installed `@earendil-works/pi-*` docs/types in `node_modules` before changing agent code. Keep those packages on one version.
- Import pi only through `src/main/agent/pi-sdk.ts` (`import()`). Never static-import pi into CJS main.
- Custom tools must be allowlisted, truncate large output, and use `withFileMutationQueue` for file writes.
- Put pi-facing tests next to the module (`src/main/agent/*.test.ts`) **locally only** — test files are gitignored and must not be committed (`Document/TESTING.md`).

## Electron (`electron-development`)

- Renderer: no Node, no filesystem. Main owns OS/DB/secrets. Preload is the only bridge.
- Keep `contextIsolation: true`, `nodeIntegration: false`. Whitelist IPC in preload; validate arguments in main.
- Native modules stay outside the bundler (`asarUnpack` / `external`), loaded at runtime.

## Desktop UI (`Document/UI_DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`)

- Dense, keyboard-first, quiet operations chrome. No marketing layouts or nested cards.
- Accent is `#13c2c2`. Terminal/code/mermaid use shared tokens. Visible focus rings; Escape closes overlays.
